@startuml ResourceQueue
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: resource admission and durable ownership of queued agent attempts
' covers: cmd/proveo/schedule.go
' covers: internal/schedule/schedule.go
' covers: internal/schedule/runner.go
' covers: internal/sbx/limits.go
' covers: internal/sbx/host_memory.go
' covers: internal/sbx/host_disk_unix.go
' covers: internal/sbx/host_disk_other.go
' covers: _spec/internal/schedule/resource_queue.qnt
' covers: cmd/proveo/admission.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/admission.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/admission_test.go
' covers: internal/schedule/queue*.go
' covers: internal/sbx/capacity.go
' covers: e2e/dashboard_admission_test.go
' status: Go admission and the durable queue are implemented.
' Quint also models disk allocation reflection; the Go ledger
' charges outstanding reservations conservatively until live qualification.
' Related capacity model: _spec/_paradigms/resource_management.puml
' Workspace and graph: _spec/internal/dashboard/workspace-instances.puml
'
' HOST CAPACITY
' Sample on the sbx host. Show CPU and system RAM as telemetry.
' Read Linux MemTotal and MemAvailable. On macOS pair hw.memsize with
' vm_stat headroom. Reuse host_memory.go's parsers.
' Record discrete VRAM as a separate per-device inference budget.
' Treat an integrated or unified GPU's shared allocations as usage of
' the same system RAM pool.
' With samples of 32 GiB system RAM and 16 GiB dedicated VRAM, verify
' the RAM total is 32 GiB. Verify a unified host reports a single RAM pool.
' Apply sbx launch limits separately from the queue's disk reservation.
' Read the reservation size on the owning host with
' sbx settings get sandbox.disk.dockerVolume. Read the structured value
' with --json and normalize it to bytes for accounting using sbx units.
' Display the configured size in its original units. Record the value
' with the reservation so a settings change applies to new launches.
' Use Unix Statfs for the daemon store and retained-artifact paths.
' The smaller free-space sample bounds admission. The daemon store sample
' drives its displayed occupied space. A same-filesystem pair has
' the same free-space limit. PROVEO_SBX_STORAGE names a custom store.
' Subtract all reservations from the configured disk pool. Subtract
' reservations pending in the measurements from available filesystem
' space. Admit against the smaller result. Confirm whether a reservation
' is reflected before excluding it from the second subtraction.
' Track disk per filesystem. A missing, stale, or unreconciled disk
' sample or unreadable reservation size pauses new admissions.
' Resample when disk capacity changes.
' Show segmented host capacity bars above the task views. Use one segment
' per 2 CPU cores, 8 GiB of RAM, or 64 GiB of disk. Show occupied capacity
' over the total, with totals in muted text. Fill partial segments in
' proportion. Include pending reservations in the disk bar.
' Show unknown occupancy when a sample is absent. Keep totals visible.
' The HTML prototype (retired 2026-11-28, decisions taken) used a 512 GiB
' disk with 180 GiB of initial headroom and a 32g sandbox.disk.dockerVolume.
'
' ADMISSION AND LIVENESS
' Serialize the disk reservation across Proveo queues on the same host.
' Record a durable disk lease before launching a job. Reconcile known VMs
' and job identities on restart. Hold leases through startup, execution,
' and result carry. An unreachable client retains its lease until
' inventory confirms the actual VM outcome.
' Release startup reservations on a verified no-start. Charge disk
' that remains to a fresh filesystem sample before admitting further
' writes. Refresh the disk sample when a reflected lease ends.
' Consider ready jobs in insertion order and take the oldest whose disk
' reservation fits. Expose wait reasons and age.
' Calendar and manual submissions persist prompt snapshots before start.
' The dispatcher samples every 5s while work remains. On shutdown it
' releases its worker lock before checking for newly submitted work.
' An installed calendar service restarts dispatch on its next tick.
' Queue items become ready through submission and prerequisite completion.
' A calendar hook can enqueue an item. It never bypasses admission.
' Runtime time limits and probe freshness still use clocks.
' Insufficient disk space and unmet prerequisites keep a task queued.
' Invalid dependency graphs or unsatisfiable requests require attention.
' Keep workflow phase separate from admission state.
'
' QUINT EVALUATION
' resource_queue.qnt models two jobs, disk headroom, and which leases
' the sample reflects. Use Quint in verification
' to check that legal transitions respect the policy pool, keep reflected
' leases attached to held work, and honor prerequisites before admission.
' The scenarios cover disk pressure, unavailable samples, exact capacity,
' pending and reflected reservations, carry, resample, and prerequisites.
' Eight Quint scenarios passed. Apalache checked all three invariants
' through 12 transitions without a violation.
' Keep the live scheduler in Go. The model abstracts OS readings, fsync,
' lifecycle discovery and simultaneous processes. Cover those boundaries
' with Go adapter tests and live sbx verification.
' Command: npx --yes @informalsystems/quint@0.34.0 test resource_queue.qnt
' Source: https://quint.sh/docs/getting-started

title Resource-driven task admission

state "Queued\nwait for prerequisites or disk" as Queued
state "Reserved\nhold configured disk before launch" as Reserved
state "Running\nhold through execution" as Running
state "Settling\nhold through outcome and Git carry" as Settling
state "Attention required\nreview, failure or invalid request" as Attention
state "Complete\naccepted work" as Complete

[*] --> Queued : submit
Queued --> Reserved : prerequisites cleared and disk fits
Queued --> Attention : invalid graph or request
Reserved --> Running : VM and agent started
Reserved --> Attention : launch failed and no VM holds lease
Running --> Settling : agent stopped or outcome recovered
Settling --> Attention : results published or operator input needed
Attention --> Queued : operator requeues
Attention --> Complete : work accepted
Complete --> [*]
@enduml
